261c8a773d3","file":"preprints/An-exact-Hausdorff-gauge-for-SLE-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":38,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"81d5a647fad3172a7404339143071d1c93d74d3a059e5783ac261ffd6058162d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-exact-Hausdorff-gauge-for-SLE-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:20845502343417c73f2765a413b83ca6367ec6d83c98e8bcb75d1261c8a773d3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-exact-Hausdorff-gauge-for-SLE-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L38"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFix $0<\\kappa<8$, and let $\\gamma$ be chordal $\\SLE_\\kappa$ from\n$0$ to $\\infty$ in the upper half-plane $\\HH$, parametrized by half-plane capacity $2t$.\nThere is a deterministic Hausdorff gauge $h_\\kappa$, depending only on\n$\\kappa$, such that almost surely, simultaneously for every real\n$0<s<t<\\infty$,\n\\[\n 0<\\Haus^{h_\\kappa}(\\gamma([s,t]))<\\infty.\n\\]"}
